         associated with the glancing impact load scenario are functions of the hull angles measured
         at the upper ice waterline (UIWL). The influence of the hull angles is captured through
         calculation of a bow shape coefficient (fa). The hull angles are defined in Figure 2.

                                        Figure 2 - Definition of hull angles




         Note:  = normal frame angle at upper ice waterline [deg]
                = upper ice waterline angle [deg]
                = buttock angle at upper ice waterline (angle of buttock line measured from horizontal) [deg]
               tan() = tan()/tan()
               tan() = tan()ꞏcos()


